  "notes": "USAGE:\n- {空々|そらぞら}しい{嘘|うそ} (an obvious lie)\n- {空々|そらぞら}しい{態度|たいど} (feigned attitude)\n- {空々|そらぞら}しく (adverb: insincerely)\nStrongly implies that the falseness is transparent to observers. The speaker can see through the pretense. Often used critically.\n\nETYMOLOGY:\nFrom {空|そら} (empty, sky) - the sense of \"empty\" or \"hollow\" giving rise to the meaning of insincerity.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {白々|しらじら}しい (feigned, pretending not to know)\n- {見|み}え{透|す}いた (transparent, obvious)\n- {取|と}って{付|つ}けた (contrived, tacked-on)",
